#!/bin/sh
# Strata session-start hook — managed by `strata register`.
#
# A Claude Code `SessionStart` hook — the READ-side trigger for shared
# memory, symmetric with the `strata-stop-hook` WRITE-side trigger beside it.
# Nothing fires on its own to make an agent read its perspective at session
# start; static instructions compete with everything else in context and
# lose. This hook prints one short instruction to stdout, which the harness
# injects as session context: read your perspective before your first
# substantive answer. It never prints memory content itself — only the
# instruction to go read it, plus the fleet's scope ids when cheaply
# available, so an unbound session's ask is concrete. No database access, no
# LLM call, no judging. It degrades silently on any error — a broken hook
# must never break the session.
#
# This wrapper `exec`s the installed engine so PATH resolution matches
# `strata-mcp`; the JSON payload on stdin flows through unchanged. All logic
# lives in `strata session-start-hook` so the engine ships exactly one
# implementation.
exec strata session-start-hook
